Why Companies Use Salesforce?
Salesforce is the market leader in CRM because it goes beyond just being a database. Companies choose it for several strategic reasons:

1.Cloud-Based Accessibility: 
        Being a cloud pioneer, Salesforce allows employees to access data from anywhere on any device. There is no         need for heavy hardware or complex local installations.

2.Scalability: 
        Whether a company is a startup with 5 employees or a global enterprise with 50,000, Salesforce can grow            with them. You can add new features and users without disrupting the current workflow.

3.Automation & Efficiency: 
        It handles repetitive manual tasks (like sending follow-up emails or routing leads to the right                    salesperson) so employees can focus on high-value work like closing deals or solving complex customer              issues.
4.Data-Driven Decisions: 
        With built-in AI (like Salesforce Einstein) and powerful reporting tools, companies can predict future             sales trends and identify exactly where their business needs to improve
